    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize explanations (e.g., adapting proofs to student’s comfort level) or generate interactive problems tailored to gaps. For example, they could flag misconceptions mid-solution or suggest analogies from literature/computer science (my hat subjects). My low openness might resist rigid curricula, but LLMs’ adaptability could bridge that gap—especially for part-time learners like me."
